WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.301
Today, as I see it today, my wish
is to stay there in the neighbourhood,

2
00:00:04.385 --> 00:00:07.023
for basic conditions so we can stay there,

3
00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:09.049
and so we pay what we have to pay.

4
00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.730
Because some think we came to build

5
00:00:11.814 --> 00:00:16.246
our little house there just
to gain rights. But it wasn't by chance.

6
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.407
Or it's some who don't know us,
or don't live among us.

7
00:00:19.491 --> 00:00:22.828
We want to stay in our neighbourhood,
in our own shack,

8
00:00:22.912 --> 00:00:26.147
and for some small conditions
to be created. Help with building?

9
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.965
None,
because we don't need help with building,

10
00:00:30.049 --> 00:00:31.932
we don't need help with the road.

11
00:00:32.016 --> 00:00:36.953
We just need peace, or a green light,
to get on with our work.

12
00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:41.888
We just need them to give us the chance
to live there with electricity

13
00:00:42.118 --> 00:00:44.868
as it should be,
and with water as it should be.

14
00:00:44.952 --> 00:00:49.269
Sometimes there isn't a drop of water
from the tap, and if you try later,

15
00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:53.056
it still doesn't drip. Some days
the water doesn't work, some days...

16
00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:57.826
it depends on how each day goes.
We have no water, no electricity.

17
00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.075
We want to ask for better conditions,
and we're ready to cooperate.

18
00:01:02.159 --> 00:01:06.211
Because there's always someone
there who works, naturally.

19
00:01:06.295 --> 00:01:08.832
The material we use
is what's normally used.

20
00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:12.645
So we're simply illegal
because the land isn't ours.

21
00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:14.670
But we're using proper materials.

22
00:01:15.807 --> 00:01:17.818
We don't have good foundations,

23
00:01:17.908 --> 00:01:21.920
because our house doesn't go up: our house
is only meant to have a metal roof.

24
00:01:22.004 --> 00:01:25.181
Apartment blocks use
better foundations than ours,

25
00:01:25.265 --> 00:01:28.262
because there they have
to stack one floor on top of another.

26
00:01:28.346 --> 00:01:31.649
We build one level, for a metal roof,
which isn't that heavy.

27
00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:35.704
That's why our foundations
are hollow block and concrete.

28
00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:39.866
Instead of bricks or blocks on top,
a metal roof goes straight on.

29
00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.993
Because that's what allows
us to go much further too.

30
00:01:43.077 --> 00:01:45.274
We're given time under pressure, in fear.

31
00:01:45.358 --> 00:01:49.635
We have to build fast to get the roof on,
and sometimes it's badly done,

32
00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:52.630
because of the pressure we feel from them.

33
00:01:52.715 --> 00:01:54.766
If you have the means,

34
00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:58.448
you'll find it easier
to build in a much better way.

35
00:01:58.532 --> 00:02:03.316
But sadly, if you're worrying about that,
you can't have that peace of mind,

36
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.792
not even in how you spend your money.

37
00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:08.313
You borrow from the bank, from a friend,

38
00:02:08.403 --> 00:02:12.480
and you're afraid to spend it,
because your heart is so tight.

39
00:02:13.206 --> 00:02:17.164
You stay put, they come, knock it down,
and you're left with the debt,

40
00:02:17.248 --> 00:02:21.380
and still no house. It's a lot.
People there are ill because of it.

41
00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:26.383
There are people who put in the door,
and today the machine hits the house:

42
00:02:27.094 --> 00:02:29.685
smashes the roof,
smashes the door, and leaves.

43
00:02:29.802 --> 00:02:33.508
That person is still without a house,
and now still has the debt.

44
00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:36.390
Imagine that person's life.

45
00:02:37.241 --> 00:02:40.278
If you go somewhere to try
to find a place, it's taken.

46
00:02:40.362 --> 00:02:45.115
Under the bridge, it's all full.
In a wood over there, it's all full.

47
00:02:45.199 --> 00:02:49.979
Sometimes people even get ill in the head,
because of this situation.

48
00:02:50.063 --> 00:02:51.710
That's my point of view.
